Sail 0.20.3 (sail @ opam-v2.5.0 0.20.3)
  --plugin <file>                           load a Sail plugin
Options for target lean
  --lean                                    invoke the Sail lean target
  --lean-output-dir <directory>             set a custom directory to output generated Lean
  --lean-force-output                       removes the content of the output directory if it is non-empty
  --lean-single-file                        puts the entire output in a single .lean file
  --lean-matchbv                            use matchbv in the Lean output
  --lean-line-width <width>                 maximum line length of the generated Lean code
  --lean-noncomputable                      add a 'noncomputable section' at the beginning of the output
  --lean-real-numbers                       enable real numbers (in particular, depend on mathlib)
  --lean-extern-type <typename>             do not generate a definition for the type
  --lean-import-file <file>                 import this file in the generated model
  --lean-noncomputable-function <func-name> do not generate executable code for this function
  --lean-partial-function <func-name>       disable the totality check for this function
  --lean-non-beq-type <func-name>           disable deriving a BEq instance for this type
  --lean-executable                         generate an executable if there is a main function in the Sail program
  --lean-lib-path <path>                    (local) path of the Lean support library, for development
  --lean-lib-repo <url>                     url of the git repository of the Lean support library
  --lean-lib-rev <revision>                 revision of the Lean support library 
